0..79 Comment "//! `buffer-returned` returns an allocated buffer after a mock ring completion."
80..83 Comment "//!"
84..155 Comment "//! It keeps a buffer live exactly once from allocation to freeing. The"
156..228 Comment "//! pathological twin refuses a buffer that a program does not return as"
229..252 Comment "//! `BufferUnreturned`."
253..256 Comment "//!"
257..331 Comment "//! A `Ring.Eff` handler mints the buffer and handles its return. The mock"
332..389 Comment "//! kernel sends it back before the continuation resumes."
390..393 Comment "//!"
394..456 Comment "//! - see: corpus/pathological/completion/buffer-misused.gandr"
457..504 Comment "//! - see: https://without.boats/blog/io-uring/"
506..549 Comment "// The native buffer a receive places live."
